# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production build configuration (used by `yarn build`, NODE_ENV=production).
#
# This file is COMMITTED on purpose. `.env` is gitignored, so it never
# reaches a CI/Render build — without these values a production bundle
# compiles with `undefined` for every REACT_APP_* variable, and API
# calls then resolve against the frontend's own origin instead of the
# backend. Keeping the production values here means a production build
# is correct by default, from any machine or CI runner.
#
# CRA precedence for a production build, first match wins:
#   .env.production.local  (gitignored — personal overrides)
#   .env.local             (gitignored)
#   .env.production        <- this file
#   .env                   (gitignored — local dev only)
# A real environment variable set by the host (Render -> Environment)
# still overrides all of the above, so the dashboard remains the place
# to change production config without a commit.
#
# Only public values belong here: everything in REACT_APP_* is readable
# by anyone who loads the site. The Supabase service-role key, the JWT
# secret and the Gemini key are backend-only and must never appear.
#
# Point local development at a local backend via `.env` (or
# .env.development.local) — e.g. REACT_APP_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001.
# Neither file is read by a production build, so doing so cannot leak a
# localhost URL into production.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# No trailing slash and no /api suffix — lib/api.js appends /api itself.
REACT_APP_BACKEND_URL=https://inventory-site-uae.onrender.com

REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL=https://utvaeusnwgzzenucdjlg.supabase.co
